{
 "esm": "2.0.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "overlap_gated_regrid_ring_params_ode",
  "description": "A construction-time conservative regrid whose overlap join gate names RING STACKS (the one-factor `[pos, verts, coord]` envelope form, CONFORMANCE_SPEC \u00a75.5.6) computed from scalar PARAMETERS (each grid's origin and spacing), the way EarthSciDiscretizations' cartesian_cell_rings_poly builds them and reseact's NEIRegrid reads them. A 6x6 source grid of 2x2 cells tiles [0,12]x[0,12]; a 3x3 target grid of 4x4 cells starts at (1, 0.5), so the targets on the east and north edges are only partly covered and the regrid weights are not trivial. The gate's range symbols come from each ring stack's FIRST (position) axis, and the parameters that feed the rings are baked, like the parameters that feed an `on` key column (\u00a75.5.8). Before this fixture the Rust binding resolved an overlap gate only over 1-D envelope factors, so a ring-stack gate was never driven: both compilers walked the full source x target product, and on a large grid the native compiler refused the narrow phase (the overlap template's per-pair vertex reductions promoted over source x target x vertex x vertex). A_ij is the overlap_area_planar template over the candidate pairs (0 at a pruned pair); area_state and regrid_state integrate the sliver-filtered row sum A_j and the regrid F_tgt of F_src = i from zero over one unit of time.",
  "authors": [
   "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
  ],
  "tags": [
   "conformance",
   "join",
   "overlap",
   "geometry",
   "overlap_area_planar",
   "construction",
   "scale"
  ]
 },
 "index_sets": {
  "src_cells": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": 36
  },
  "tgt_cells": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": 9
  },
  "verts": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": 4
  },
  "coord": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": 2
  }
 },
 "models": {
  "OverlapGatedRegridRingParams": {
   "expression_template_imports": [
